what Row 7's second erratum closed on a named next step nobody has taken: name which FILES sit on which node rather than which modules, since 34,941,409 tracked Rye bytes over 16 nodes overflow every module assignment while the largest single file is a quarter of a node's share. Measured before claiming rather than reasoned: 1,761 non-symlink Rye sources carry 7,616 distinct file-to-file import edges over 1,563 endpoint files, against the room graph's 68 pairs, and 6,401 of those 7,616 -- 84 percent -- sit INSIDE one room, so they are invisible to the room graph and free by construction under any module placement. The file unit also has its own ceiling the erratum never names: an equal share is 2,194,604 bytes at 16 nodes and 548,651 at 64, while the largest file is 568,249, so the unit fits at 4 and 16 nodes and overflows at 64. This lap builds one scan reading three things -- where the unit stops fitting, what the finer graph holds against the room graph, and whether a capacity-constrained greedy file placement beats a size-matched random baseline on the same occupancy -- with its own pen and witness, and one Field paper. Touches no peer file, no module source, no existing scan, no ceiling any peer watches and no ledger row; tools/fixtures/a/aurora_placement_scan.sh is READ and never edited.
